        "comment": [
          "  /*",
          "   * Atmosphere: one light source, and the texture it reveals. Decorative only.",
          "   * Every value here is painted on a pseudo-element behind the content or as a",
          "   * shadow around it - never as a text colour, and never as a translucent",
          "   * background a text token would have to be measured against. The two layers",
          "   * that do fall under text, the hero lamp and the panel glaze, are checked at",
          "   * their peak alpha by `tests/a11y/tokenContrast.test.ts`.",
          "   *",
          "   * Light mode is not dark mode with the numbers flipped, and it is not the",
          "   * same numbers either. Both themes ADD light at the lamp and fall back to",
          "   * their own ground away from it - which means the atmosphere can only ever",
          "   * lift a pale canvas towards white and deepen a near-black one towards black.",
          "   * Neither theme can push a background past a value the gate above already",
          "   * checks. That is a property, not a coincidence: a lamp that tinted this",
          "   * canvas *darker* would drop text-subtle, which clears the plain canvas with",
          "   * limited headroom and has nowhere to go.",
          "   */"
        ],
